A newspaper wants a short comparison of the Pandharpur wari and the Sabarimala pilgrimage for its weekend page. Using the chapter, compare them under four heads:
(a) the place and the deity each pilgrimage goes to;
(b) one number the chapter gives for each;
(c) how pilgrims traditionally travel in each;
(d) one idea about pilgrimage that both share.

Anita lives in central India and sets out on the char dham yatra. Using the chapter, explain:
(a) why her journey will take her across the length and breadth of the country;
(b) two kinds of differences she is likely to meet along the way;
(c) one other network of sacred places that, like the char dham, is spread across India.
